4.ARRAY SUBSET
Given two arrays a[] and b[], your task is to determine whether b[] is a subset of a[].
SOURCE CODE :
				class Solution {
			    public boolean isSubset(int a[], int b[]) {
			        Arrays.sort(a);
			        Arrays.sort(b);
			        int i=0,j=0;
			        if(a.length<b.length){
			            return false;
			        }
			        while(i<a.length && j<b.length){
			            if(a[i]<b[j]){
			                i++; 
			            } 
			            else if(a[i]==b[j]){
			                i++;
			                j++; 
			            } 
			            else{
			                return false; 
			            }
			        }
			        return j==b.length;
			    }
				}
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/array-subset-of-another-array2317/1


5.VALUE EQUAL TO POSITION
Given an array arr[]. Find the elements whose value is equal to the position where they appear.
SOURCE CODE :
				class Solution {
				    public static ArrayList<Integer> valEqualToPos(int[] arr) {
				        ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
				        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
				            if(arr[i]==(i+1)){
				                list.add(arr[i]);
				            }
				        }
				        return list;
				    }
				}
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/value-equal-to-index-value1330/1


6.ROTATE ARRAY BY ONE
Given an array arr, rotate the array by one position in clockwise direction.
SOURCE CODE :
				class Solution {
				    public void rotate(int[] arr) {
				        int temp=arr[arr.length-1];
				        for(int i=arr.length-1;i>0;i--){
				            arr[i]=arr[i-1];
				        }
				        arr[0]=temp;
				    }
				}
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/cyclically-rotate-an-array-by-one2614/1


